      "translation_input": "During a dust storm on 18 October 2025, solar output fell by 34 percent in 15 minutes Battery-cabinet temperature rose by 8 degrees Celsius. and the inverter fan developed an unusual low- frequency vibration The controller did not shut down the entire station. It disconnected secondary heaters, reduced selected lighting, started the 0 backup generator, and issued a maintenance warning Diagnostic software identified three plausible faults debris covering part of the solar array. wear in a fan bearing. and increasing contact resistance at a battery connector These possibilities were ranked, but none was presented as certain because the measurements could be explained by more than one physical condition",
